/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - The main parts of a dumpy level are the telescope (objective lens, eyepiece, and the diaphragm carrying the cross-hairs), the focusing screw, the bubble tube (a curved vial whose axis is horizontal when the bubble is central), the levelling
   - Three lines matter.
   - Permanent adjustments correct the instrument itself, in this order:
   - The two-peg test uses two pegs A and B about 100 m apart:
   - a₁, b₁ are the readings on A and B from the midpoint; a₂, b₂ the readings from D; DA, DB the distances from D to A and B in metres.
   - The sensitivity of a bubble tube is the angle the line of sight tilts when the bubble moves one division.
*/
